## 3. Semantic Schema Profiling & Long-Term Memory

A core architectural feature of the platform is its **AI-Driven Semantic Schema Profiler** and **Long-Term Memory** system. When a database table is created or ingested (e.g. "Components", "Responsibles"), the AI profiles each column and saves the schema definition in `agent_memories`.

### The Semantic Schema Profile Specification

Each table profile in `agent_memories` under `table_schema:<table_name>` contains:

```json
{
  "table_name": "components",
  "description": "Database table for components.",
  "target_fields": ["componentname", "modelname", "supplier", "freq", "id_responsible", "docinfo_link"],
  "columns": {
    "componentname": { "semantic_type": "text", "label": "Component Name" },
    "modelname": { "semantic_type": "text", "label": "Model Name" },
    "supplier": { "semantic_type": "supplier", "label": "Supplier" },
    "freq": { "semantic_type": "text", "label": "Frequency" },
    "id_responsible": { "semantic_type": "email", "label": "Responsible Person" },
    "docinfo_link": { "semantic_type": "url", "label": "DocInfo Link" }
  },
  "registered_at": "2026-09-06T16:56:50Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-09-06T16:58:30Z"
}
```

### Supported Semantic Types

| Semantic Type | Purpose & Behavior | UI Widget / Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| `email` | Responsible engineer contacts, LDAP addresses, notification recipients | Clickable `mailto:` link with Mail icon |
| `url` | PDF document links, regulatory certification portals, external specs | Clickable `https://` external link with ExternalLink icon |
| `date` | Certification issue/expiration timestamps, audit dates | ISO 8601 formatting (`YYYY-MM-DD`) |
| `phone` | International support & contact numbers | E.164 standardization |
| `supplier` | Automotive Tier-1 suppliers and manufacturers | Canonical alias lookup |
| `badge` | Status tags, abbreviations, priority flags | Visual tag / pill |
| `number` | Numerical metrics, frequencies, validity years | Number input & sorting |
| `text` | General names, model designations, descriptions | Standard editable cell |

### Elimination of Brittle Regex Heuristics

Rather than applying fragile client-side keyword lists or regexes on cell contents at render time, the frontend data grid deterministically reads `col.semantic_type` directly from the schema API (`/api/v1/schema/tables/{table}/data`). The AI serves as the single source of truth for semantic meaning across both built-in core tables and user-defined custom tables.

