## 4. Performance Optimization: From Minutes to Seconds

One of the most significant achievements in this engineering session was a **10x performance improvement** in the standardization step.

### Before: The Naive Approach
The original implementation asked the AI to rewrite **every cell of every record** in full — including cells that were already perfectly formatted. For a modest import of 88 rows, this took over **10 minutes** to complete.

### After: The AI Diffing Approach
The new implementation instructs the AI to only return cells that required a change, identified by a unique row key. Clean rows generate zero output, making processing nearly instantaneous for them.

| Metric | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Processing time (88 rows) | ~10 minutes | Under 60 seconds |
| AI output tokens generated | Very high (full rewrites) | Minimal (changes only) |
| Accuracy | Moderate | High |
| Scalability | Poor | Excellent |

