## 5. Data Integrity & Safety Mechanisms

The pipeline was designed with multiple layers of protection to ensure that no data is silently lost or corrupted:

### Flexible Identifier Normalization (`norm_to_col`)
Spreadsheet headers frequently vary in spacing and casing (e.g. `"Component Name"`, `"component_name"`, `"componentname"`, `"DocInfo Link"`). The backend normalization engine normalizes all keys and maps them directly to the underlying PostgreSQL columns, preventing SQL syntax errors and schema mismatches.

### SQL Column Deduplication Guard
During bulk insertion, column identifiers are strictly deduplicated in SQL generation, eliminating `psycopg2.errors.DuplicateColumn` errors when raw headers and mapped targets co-exist in an import payload.

### Hyperlink Artifact Sanitization
Excel exports often contain embedded hyperlink metadata (e.g. `user@domain.com#mailto:user@domain.com#`). The system automatically strips internal hyperlink artifacts, storing clean data in PostgreSQL while maintaining interactive `mailto:` links in the UI.

### Unmapped Column Guardrail
If an uploaded file contains columns that have no correspondence in the target table, the import does not fail silently. The system:
1. Notifies the user of the unmapped columns.
2. Requests explicit permission to create new columns.
3. Proceeds only after user confirmation.

### No Cloud Data Exposure
The AI processing is entirely on-premise, running on a dedicated GCP NVIDIA L4 GPU instance (24 GB VRAM). No user data is transmitted to any external AI service.

